// spec: FUN-006
//
// ⚠️ A defect is a statement about the INTERPRETER and is never compiled.
//
// A parameter is an assignment context [VAR-017], so each of these calls must
// be refused.  None is: only the arity is checked, because a top-level
// subprogram does not overload and nothing ever compares its parameters.
//
// ⚠️ The same signature AS A METHOD refuses all three -- refusals/0025.  The
// annotation is a contract in one place and decoration in the other.

function G (N : Integer); begin Exit N; end

WriteLn (G ('a string'));
WriteLn (G (1.5));
WriteLn (G (True));
